## Best Practices

### Version Numbering
- Start at 1.0.0 for public launch
- Use 0.x.x for pre-release/beta
- Increment logically (don't skip numbers)

### Changelog Writing
- Be specific about changes
- Use active voice
- Include context (why, not just what)
- Reference related nodes with wiki-links
- Keep bilingual consistency

### Release Timing
- Batch related changes
- Avoid releases during high traffic
- Test thoroughly before release
- Coordinate with content updates

### Git Tags
- Never delete tags (unless absolutely necessary)
- Use 'v' prefix (v1.0.2)
- Keep in sync with versions.json

## Success Criteria

- Version synchronized across all files
- GitHub Actions passing
- Deployment successful
- Release created with correct tag
- Site accessible and functional
- Changelog accurate and bilingual
- No broken links or 404s
